{"agent":"cc1-kilo","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new `try: fd = os.open(...); except OSError: continue` treats every open failure as “not a shard”. Given a regular shard `0.jsonl` that contains the event id being rewritten but cannot be opened for reading because of `PermissionError`, `EMFILE`, `EIO`, etc., the code silently continues to the next shard. If no later shard contains the id, `_rewrite_line` returns without replacing the line and without raising; if a later shard contains a duplicate, it rewrites that and returns, leaving the old line in the skipped real shard. The previous MEDIUM finding still holds: the handler is not narrowed to “vanished/symlink/FIFO” errors.","digest":"00178e755df9baac","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The no-follow read only protects `os.open`, not the read. Given `.ddflow/events/a.jsonl` created as a FIFO and another process holding its write end with no bytes written, `shards()` returns it (it is not a symlink), `shard.is_symlink()` is false, and `os.open(..., O_RDONLY | O_NOFOLLOW | O_NONBLOCK)` succeeds. `fh.read()` then raises `BlockingIOError` (an `OSError`) outside the `try`, so `_rewrite_line` aborts instead of skipping the FIFO; any line in a later shard is not rewritten. The `O_NONBLOCK` change does not answer the previous FIFO probe.","digest":"bdbb31c5859d40e1","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"In `_rewrite_line`, `os.open(shard, os.O_RDONLY | os.O_NOFOLLOW | os.O_NONBLOCK)` raises an `OSError` if `shard` is a symlink. Since `shards()` already filters out symlinks, a TOCTOU race where a real file is swapped for a symlink between `shards()` and `os.open` will be caught and silently skipped. However, if `shard` is a FIFO (which is not a symlink, so `shards()` returns it), `os.open` with `O_NONBLOCK` on the read end of a FIFO with no writers succeeds, but then reading from it via `fh.read()` on an empty FIFO returns immediately as empty string. More importantly, if `shard` is a directory or a regular file that triggers a permission error, `os.open` raises an `OSError` and the exception handler silently swallows it, ignoring real readable files that encounter permission errors.","digest":"7f7557b07a938961","family":"google","location":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:493","malformed":"","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:493"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The new `except OSError: continue` around `os.open` is still too broad, so a real shard that cannot be opened is treated as “no line here.” `PermissionError`, `IsADirectoryError`, and `EMFILE` are all `OSError`. Given `.ddflow/events/0.jsonl` as a regular file that contains the event id to rewrite but is mode `000`, `os.open(..., O_RDONLY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK)` raises `PermissionError`, the handler skips the shard, and `_rewrite_line` raises `KeyError` as if the line were absent instead of failing the rewrite.","digest":"690f9b04df149647","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"The no-follow open still only skips `OSError` from `os.open`. A FIFO is not a symlink, so `shards()` still returns it and `is_symlink()` is false. `os.open(..., O_RDONLY|O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK)` succeeds when another process holds the write end and has written nothing; `fh.read()` then raises `BlockingIOError` (an `OSError`) outside that `try`, so the rewrite aborts instead of skipping. Given `.ddflow/events/a.jsonl` as a FIFO held open for write, a rewrite of an id that is not in that FIFO crashes rather than continuing.","digest":"85280356e0b705dc","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line"}],"chunks_total":1,"coverage":"1/1 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":1,"diff_chars":7050,"diff_sha":"7930566ff48b7ca51b47788c07af66aa0674500a072e8e337a787ad3cea96e29","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B143a77ee1d","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":7.2,"family":"alibaba","findings":5,"max_chunk_chars":12000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"0ffd36353aa6ae3a","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B143a77ee1d.rubber_duck.gemini-3.5-flash-lite.20261112T134308Z-71d94f0b.jsonl","passed_on_refutation":{"confirmed":2,"max_rounds":6,"refuted":3,"rounds":6},"reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1],"reviewed_head":"dbb01892575ab200fbc1fbb41654722835d0c30c","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py":"100644 b1da0f12bec2960c1a821c3a9cef8768b68e4bc8","tests/test_shard_symlink.py":"100644 97250c27d8cc0d86645919b4285405b8234ef6de"},"reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","reviewer_digest":"3926c0df5644d7de","reviewer_families":["alibaba","google","xai"],"round":5,"rounds":5,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line","ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line","ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:493","ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line","ddflow/infra/log/_eventlog.py:_rewrite_line"],"tree_sha":"dbb01892575a+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":""},"id":"e5b76758baa3d308dd32c31c6","kind":"gate.passed","lamport":183496,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B143a77ee1d","ts":"2026-11-12T13:47:50.070072Z"}
